  The same terms are stated in the data itself. The _meta block at the head of each of Features.json, Instructions.json and
  Registers.json reads:

    "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2010-2026 Arm Limited or its affiliates. All rights reserved."
    "info": "This document is Non-confidential and licensed under the BSD 3-clause license."

  The README.md of the package reads:

    This package contains a subset of the information provided in the packages with Arm proprietary licenses. Content that is not
    currently in a machine-readable format, as well as all descriptive content, is omitted.

    The [notice](docs/notice.html) gives details of the license terms and conditions under which this package is provided.

what the conditions mean for masc
  1 and 2: the licence text and the copyright line travel with the vendored copy in gen/vendor/aarchmrs/LICENSE and in masc's NOTICE,
  which is shipped with masc in source and binary form.
  3: neither Arm's name nor its contributors' names are used to endorse masc.

